{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789342910,"nonce":"vx4OVqIl+9DM/SazJTJ55+h5taQ=","title":"A vectorized loop's exit block keeps phis naming the old header","message":"`loop_vectorize`, `reduction_vectorize` and `auto_vectorize` replace the\nedge header -\u003e exit with scalar_check -\u003e exit and fix the exit block's\npredecessor list, but not the exit block's own phis, which still name\nthe header as their incoming block. Out-of-SSA then finds no incoming\nfor the edge actually taken and the value is undefined: the interpreter\nreports \"type mismatch: expected integer, got Undef\".\n\nLatent until a3 (empty-block threading in cfg_simplify): the SSA builder\nlands every loop exit in an empty block of its own, so the exit never\nhad phis. With those blocks threaded away a loop can exit straight into\nthe next loop's header, and its phis are the ones left stale.\n\nRepro: `crates/zynml/tests/float_store_width.rs`\n(`a_scaled_store_writes_one_element_not_two`), interpreted variant.\n\nFix: rewrite the exit's phi incomings from the header to the scalar\ncheck alongside the predecessor list, in all three passes.","files":null}]}